[Music]  welcome back to cbs this morning  the mother and partner of u.s capitol  police officer brian sicknick say  they will keep fighting for a january 6  commission  the pair were on capitol hill last week  to lobby for the independent panel  which senate republicans blocked on  friday they spoke with nicole killing  about the vote  who they blame for the outcome and how  they are still coping with officer  siknik's death  after that assault on the capitol he  texted me he says  i'm busy right now i can't talk and that  was the last i  you know i heard from him it was january  6th the final time gladys sicknick would  communicate with her son  after he was attacked with chemical  spray and collapsed  his longtime companion sandra garza got  the fateful call  to rush to the hospital did you get to  say goodbye  no i did not they would not let me back  to see brian  it was only then when the emergency  physician and the  charge nurse came out to tell me that  you know he was on a ventilator  and i knew i knew then that  he wasn't fine thinking of you for  nearly  five months consolation has come through  cards from complete strangers  just when you think that the cards stop  they start  coming again from all over the country  and the world  actually what does that mean to you  that there are good people in this world  last week they finally made the decision  to speak out going door to door on  capitol hill  to demand a bipartisan commission  investigate the capital attack  we want answers and nobody nobody has  the answers i mean even the people who  voted for this  bill they don't have any answers and  it's just  sad despite their best efforts the  motion is not  agreed to they watched as the senate  struck it down  six votes short i'm disgusted  that the republican senators  that decided to vote no it's a spit in  the face  to brian it's a spit in the face to all  the officers that were there that day  did it bother you that some senators  weren't even there  absolutely that's a dereliction of duty  but their frustration  doesn't solely lie with congress so  ultimately do you blame the former  president  yes i do and i was a  person who supporter supported donald  trump  brian was a supporter of his i mean even  on brian's twitter page  he had donald trump's personal plane in  the background as his background picture  you know he was still the president at  that time and he knew that brian  was you know devoted to him and he  did not once reach out to me to gladys  he didn't even send a letter of  condolences he did absolutely nothing  and so you know it's  it's very upsetting you know that he's  not  and i would meet with him actually i  would i would meet with him  what would you say to him i would ask  him i would say  you know why didn't you reach out to us  and i would ask him why he he failed all  law enforcement that day  you know he has an opportunity to turn  this around you know if he's really  gonna back the blue  then back it up with your actions he  just watched it on television like it  was a soap opera  i don't understand it how can you be so  uncaring  would you consider filing suit against  the former president  at this time i'm not interested in doing  that  do you think both sides are to blame for  making this so political  well i think in every party you know  there's going to be politics  for me this isn't about you know being a  republican or a democrat or  it's none of that it's about doing  what's right for the country  and doing right by brian what do you  think he would make of  everything that's happening right now  well brian was very  he was a gentle soul he really was and  he  he had a work ethic that was  unbelievable  and um but don't push him in a corner so  what what happened now i think he would  be appalled but  he says it will it'll get better and it  will  i'm sure and hopefully he  brian will have left the legacy that  will help our country  i want to point out that during our  interview mrs siknik was wearing her  son's shirt and both she  and sandra were wearing necklaces that  contain  brian's ashes they say that that is a  way to keep him close and  they are still looking for ways to carry  out his legacy but they have not given  up  on a january 6 commission and they say  they plan to keep meeting with lawmakers  including congresswoman liz cheney later  today  tony unimaginable grief they have that  mission for the january 6 commission  nicole powerful interview it is  breathtaking to hear  the sicknick family and his partner  sandra talk about going from supporting  president trump to wondering where are  you mr president in the aftermath of  this  yes say something to us i appreciate  them sharing their story and say look  for them it's not democrat or republican  it's pain and  i like the message let's just do right  by brian also something as simple as the  last text had said i'm busy right now i  can't talk  such an ordinary text that takes on such  a different meaning now that we know  what he was dealing with at that time  very sad heart goes out to both of them  all right nicole thank you very much

